(4850467, 702066, 70128, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments! To answer some of them:<br/>* I couldn''t get the fire under the kettle, there was no way to paint the stove in black! LOL<br/>* I didn''t add the noise, in fact, I reduced it as much as I could. As it was still noisy, and the kettle was rather old, that''s when I thought I could give this an old look with Sepia, and that lead to the title.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-08-25 18:56:07.</i></td>', 'Thanks for the comments! To answer some of them:* I couldn''t get the fire under the kettle, there was no way to paint the stove in black! LOL* I didn''t add the noise, in fact, I reduced it as much as I could. As it was still noisy, and the kettle was rather old, that''s when I thought I could give this an old look with Sepia, and that lead to the title.', '2008-07-30 01:17:23.000000', '2008-08-25 19:56:07.000000', 0),
(4850484, 701919, 68504, '<td valign="top">Not fair.  You enjoyed this.</td>', 'Not fair.  You enjoyed this.', '2008-07-30 01:21:49.000000', NULL, 0),
