(4851187, 701580, 79955, '<td valign="top">Not sure what you used for your background , however a good way to get a really black background is to use black velvet. <br/> <br/>Another way would be to post process using Photoshop CS3 , go to Image &gt; adjust &gt; selective color. Choose the black slider &amp; move it to the right. That should blacken your background further</td>', 'Not sure what you used for your background , however a good way to get a really black background is to use black velvet.  Another way would be to post process using Photoshop CS3 , go to Image > adjust > selective color. Choose the black slider & move it to the right. That should blacken your background further', '2008-07-30 09:55:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(4851204, 701580, 49109, '<td valign="top">The problem here isn''t the not-all-black background (actually, I like how the bowl and the background are still separated), it is the shallow DOF - many viewers don''t like it, when the frontmost parts are OOF  and the long  exposure, that made the flame look kinda strange. In addition, it is clearly visible, that the flame comes from behind the chili.</td>', 'The problem here isn''t the not-all-black background (actually, I like how the bowl and the background are still separated), it is the shallow DOF - many viewers don''t like it, when the frontmost parts are OOF  and the long  exposure, that made the flame look kinda strange. In addition, it is clearly visible, that the flame comes from behind the chili.', '2008-07-30 10:00:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(4851242, 701699, 37684, '<td valign="top">I''m really surprised this didn''t place much higher!<br/> <br/>It''s a great shot.</td>', 'I''m really surprised this didn''t place much higher! It''s a great shot.', '2008-07-30 10:14:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(4851245, 701631, 81362, '<td valign="top">I like the simplicity and symmetry. A bonus point for me is seeing for the first time the detail inside this type of heating element. Perhaps the similarity to the red lamp in a traffic light makes it less easily seen as "hot". Nevertheless, I think it deserved to place much higher in the challenge.</td>', 'I like the simplicity and symmetry. A bonus point for me is seeing for the first time the detail inside this type of heating element. Perhaps the similarity to the red lamp in a traffic light makes it less easily seen as "hot". Nevertheless, I think it deserved to place much higher in the challenge.', '2008-07-30 10:16:13.000000', NULL, 0),
