(4851372, 702011, 24642, '<td valign="top">Good to see you back Jon.  Congrats on the ribbon.</td>', 'Good to see you back Jon.  Congrats on the ribbon.', '2008-07-30 15:04:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(4851374, 702142, 52115, '<td valign="top">This is a really hot picture!</td>', 'This is a really hot picture!', '2008-07-30 15:05:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(4851407, 701735, 60047, '<td valign="top">Adam, those of us who are lower down on the learning curve would love to hear how you did this.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Adam, those of us who are lower down on the learning curve would love to hear how you did this. ', '2008-07-30 15:21:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(4851410, 701580, 24896, '<td valign="top">One thing I think that kept the score average<br/> <br/>Not razor sharp..I have the same lens and love it. I find that F8-F11 are best for a setup like this. And if you want to really black out the background. Keep the subject and the background as far away from each other as you can. Dial your aperture down to the smallest opening F25/F29 depending on you focal length. Put as much light on the subject as you can while keeping off the background. This will let the shutter open and close before the light has a chance to reflect off the background and back into the camera. More light would have helped the color of the pepper POP too. <br/>I like the composition, the subject, and overall idea (I shot something very similar)<a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=701199" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">here</a>. Please PM me if you have any questions or comments</td>', 'One thing I think that kept the score average Not razor sharp..I have the same lens and love it. I find that F8-F11 are best for a setup like this. And if you want to really black out the background. Keep the subject and the background as far away from each other as you can. Dial your aperture down to the smallest opening F25/F29 depending on you focal length. Put as much light on the subject as you can while keeping off the background. This will let the shutter open and close before the light has a chance to reflect off the background and back into the camera. More light would have helped the color of the pepper POP too. I like the composition, the subject, and overall idea (I shot something very similar)here. Please PM me if you have any questions or comments', '2008-07-30 15:22:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(4851467, 701735, 96385, '<td valign="top">I loved this photo as well, but I am perplexed as to how this was done in Basic Editing and would appreciate any tips as well.</td>', 'I loved this photo as well, but I am perplexed as to how this was done in Basic Editing and would appreciate any tips as well.', '2008-07-30 16:01:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(4851522, 701756, 96385, '<td valign="top">Well I really loved this photo, and gave it a 9.  I''m a bit shocked you came in where you did. I thought your DOF gave it more of a hot look (heat wave).</td>', 'Well I really loved this photo, and gave it a 9.  I''m a bit shocked you came in where you did. I thought your DOF gave it more of a hot look (heat wave).', '2008-07-30 16:28:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(4851703, 701735, 9114, '<td valign="top">Well this is interesting and very well done. I don''t believe it''s the real sun and the black horse/rider looks like a paper cutout (or small plastic toy of some kind) silhouette. I think the specks are actual stars? I do hope you comment on how it was done. . I love to see images that make me think and wonder how it was done.<br/> <br/>Magnificent<br/>Debbi</td>', 'Well this is interesting and very well done. I don''t believe it''s the real sun and the black horse/rider looks like a paper cutout (or small plastic toy of some kind) silhouette. I think the specks are actual stars? I do hope you comment on how it was done. . I love to see images that make me think and wonder how it was done. MagnificentDebbi', '2008-07-30 18:19:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(4851938, 701720, 1024, '<td valign="top">I gave this a 6 on the cuteness factor alone.  I can not help explain the low scores.<br/></td>', 'I gave this a 6 on the cuteness factor alone.  I can not help explain the low scores.', '2008-07-30 20:15:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(4851998, 701720, 24896, '<td valign="top">I love this photo and gave it an 8. It was the best out of the box submission (IMO) that you could really see HOT in. The catch light in the eyes is great, I love that I can see the tongue in the bowl (that''s what made it for me). Only downfall IMO is the cutoff paw. Adding a little more frame to the bottom would have placed the eyes and the lip of the bowl on thirds and added a better balance IMO<br/> <br/>On a personal side, This pup reminds me of my Max, Max is a LabX (we think Great Dane). We adopted Max when he was six months old. We where the third people to take Max home and by six months he had already been so badly abused that I had to hand feed him 2-4 kibbles at a time. For almost two months to gain his trust. He is missing teeth from the abuse so his tongue hands out the side of his mouth quite often. Its quite funny to see and your photo reminded me of puppy Max. It''s been just over a year that we have had him and he is very happy and adjusting well. Still has some moments but we know how to read him.<br/> <br/>Good photo, shitty score. I think it should have done much better. Maybe its worth an OOBE!</td>', 'I love this photo and gave it an 8. It was the best out of the box submission (IMO) that you could really see HOT in. The catch light in the eyes is great, I love that I can see the tongue in the bowl (that''s what made it for me). Only downfall IMO is the cutoff paw. Adding a little more frame to the bottom would have placed the eyes and the lip of the bowl on thirds and added a better balance IMO On a personal side, This pup reminds me of my Max, Max is a LabX (we think Great Dane). We adopted Max when he was six months old. We where the third people to take Max home and by six months he had already been so badly abused that I had to hand feed him 2-4 kibbles at a time. For almost two months to gain his trust. He is missing teeth from the abuse so his tongue hands out the side of his mouth quite often. Its quite funny to see and your photo reminded me of puppy Max. It''s been just over a year that we have had him and he is very happy and adjusting well. Still has some moments but we know how to read him. Good photo, shitty score. I think it should have done much better. Maybe its worth an OOBE!', '2008-07-30 20:47:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(4852035, 701720, 27373, '<td valign="top">I did not vote on this challenge.  I think a number of people probably did not pick up on the correlation between a dog drinking water and a hot day, and therefore felt you were shoehorning in a shot of your pet with the title.  A number of the low votes probably also came from people that immediatly dismissed it as a snap shot and moved on to the next image.<br/>Thats my analysis, for what its worth.<br/></td>', 'I did not vote on this challenge.  I think a number of people probably did not pick up on the correlation between a dog drinking water and a hot day, and therefore felt you were shoehorning in a shot of your pet with the title.  A number of the low votes probably also came from people that immediatly dismissed it as a snap shot and moved on to the next image.Thats my analysis, for what its worth.', '2008-07-30 21:05:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(4852124, 701096, 88136, '<td valign="top">who seriously gave this a 2?</td>', 'who seriously gave this a 2?', '2008-07-30 21:44:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(4852176, 702007, 83313, '<td valign="top">I think the main reason this came in so low is that it is very abstract. (refer to my "point of color" entry to see a similar scoring performance!) Abstracts normally don''t score very well here. Not everybody appreciates abstract photography and scores here are a measure of broad appeal. I think perhaps the glow of the rebar hides the detail that would let someone know what it is, so it is taken as an abstract image.</td>', 'I think the main reason this came in so low is that it is very abstract. (refer to my "point of color" entry to see a similar scoring performance!) Abstracts normally don''t score very well here. Not everybody appreciates abstract photography and scores here are a measure of broad appeal. I think perhaps the glow of the rebar hides the detail that would let someone know what it is, so it is taken as an abstract image.', '2008-07-30 22:07:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(4852216, 701451, 33672, '<td valign="top">Terry, This is great. Almost neo-nostalgic. great great work! You were definitely robbed.</td>', 'Terry, This is great. Almost neo-nostalgic. great great work! You were definitely robbed.', '2008-07-30 22:25:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(4852228, 701720, 79720, '<td valign="top">I didn''t vote in this challenge, but in all honesty I probably would have given it a 5 and moved on. I suppose it''s a nice dog, if you like dogs, but someone has already mentioned the "snapshot" feel. There seems to be a lack of contrast, maybe even a bit of white-balance imbalance. The composition is so-so, but there isn''t anything that keeps my interest for very long. Even with all that, a dog with it''s face in a water dish doesn''t necessarily make me think "hot" any more so than a dog with a doggie-coat might make me think "cold".<br/> <br/>Please don''t take this as mean-spirited, or intentionally over-critical, but I could see how someone might vote this a low score. I very rarely hand out anything lower than a 3 (I wouldn''t have, in this case), but that''s me. There are some very picky voters out there.</td>', 'I didn''t vote in this challenge, but in all honesty I probably would have given it a 5 and moved on. I suppose it''s a nice dog, if you like dogs, but someone has already mentioned the "snapshot" feel. There seems to be a lack of contrast, maybe even a bit of white-balance imbalance. The composition is so-so, but there isn''t anything that keeps my interest for very long. Even with all that, a dog with it''s face in a water dish doesn''t necessarily make me think "hot" any more so than a dog with a doggie-coat might make me think "cold". Please don''t take this as mean-spirited, or intentionally over-critical, but I could see how someone might vote this a low score. I very rarely hand out anything lower than a 3 (I wouldn''t have, in this case), but that''s me. There are some very picky voters out there.', '2008-07-30 22:30:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(4852322, 701559, 67697, '<td valign="top">This is wicked cooool.  Congrats on the ribbon!</td>', 'This is wicked cooool.  Congrats on the ribbon!', '2008-07-30 23:04:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(4852439, 702134, 67697, '<td valign="top">I''m surprised at no comments.  I''ve been wanting to try something like this where the flower is lit from the back and you capture the inner glow.  That part is cool.  The trick is how do you get that center part in focus and that''s just something I don''t know how to do lol.  That inner glowy part is gorgeous!</td>', 'I''m surprised at no comments.  I''ve been wanting to try something like this where the flower is lit from the back and you capture the inner glow.  That part is cool.  The trick is how do you get that center part in focus and that''s just something I don''t know how to do lol.  That inner glowy part is gorgeous!', '2008-07-30 23:35:17.000000', NULL, 0),
